# Windows runs the same Cabal command as the Unix BUILD. This replaces a recipe that
# ran Cabal only if %ProgramFiles%\cabal\bin\cabal.exe existed. The setup step
# installs Cabal with ghcup under C:\ghcup\bin, so that file never exists on the
# runner, the recipe printed "cabal not found -- skipping", and the package passed
# without running a single test (it finished in under a second). A missing cabal
# now fails visibly. Each line of a BUILD file runs in its own shell, so the
# command stays on one line.
cabal test all --test-show-details=direct
